# engineering.kb — designing and building things that have to hold up.
#
# The domain is deliberately written around `purpose`, `requires` and `causes` rather than around
# names, because what makes engineering a subject is the reasoning from load to failure and from
# requirement to design, and a store of nouns cannot answer any of it.

engineering | is_a=discipline | purpose=designing things that solve a problem within real constraints | has_kind=civil engineering | has_kind=mechanical engineering | has_kind=electrical engineering | has_kind=chemical engineering | has_kind=software engineering | has_kind=aerospace engineering
civil engineering | is_a=engineering | purpose=designing roads, bridges, dams and buildings
mechanical engineering | is_a=engineering | purpose=designing machines and the parts that move
electrical engineering | is_a=engineering | purpose=designing circuits, power systems and electronics
chemical engineering | is_a=engineering | purpose=designing processes that transform materials at scale
aerospace engineering | is_a=engineering | purpose=designing aircraft and spacecraft

# --- the reasoning ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
design | is_a=activity | purpose=choosing a form that meets the requirements | requires=a statement of the requirements | requires=knowledge of the materials
requirement | is_a=stated need a design must meet | purpose=making it possible to tell whether a design succeeded
constraint | is_a=limit a design must respect | has_kind=cost | has_kind=weight | has_kind=time | has_kind=safety
trade off | is_a=situation | occurs_when=improving one property worsens another | causes=a choice that has to be justified
safety factor | is_a=ratio | means=how much stronger a thing is built than the worst expected load | purpose=covering what the calculation did not know | causes=heavier and costlier structures
tolerance | is_a=allowed deviation from a stated dimension | purpose=letting parts made separately still fit
specification | is_a=written description of what is to be built | purpose=letting the builder and the buyer mean the same thing
prototype | is_a=early working version | purpose=finding out what the drawing did not say | causes=design changes before manufacture
failure analysis | is_a=activity | purpose=finding why something broke | causes=a design change | requires=the broken part

# --- loads and failure -------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
load | is_a=force a structure must carry | has_kind=dead load | has_kind=live load | has_kind=wind load
dead load | is_a=load | means=the permanent weight of the structure itself
live load | is_a=load | means=the changing weight of people and things using the structure
stress | is_a=physical quantity | means=force divided by the area carrying it | unit=pascal | causes=strain
strain | is_a=physical quantity | means=the fractional change in length under stress
tension | is_a=stress that pulls a material apart | causes=stretching
compression | is_a=stress that pushes a material together | causes=shortening | causes=buckling in a slender member
shear | is_a=stress that slides one part of a material past another
bending | is_a=combination of tension and compression across a beam | occurs_when=a beam carries a load between its supports
buckling | is_a=sudden sideways failure | occurs_when=a slender column is compressed beyond a critical load | causes=collapse
fatigue | is_a=failure mode | occurs_when=a material is loaded and unloaded many times | causes=a crack that grows with each cycle | causes=failure far below the static strength
creep | is_a=failure mode | occurs_when=a material is held under load at high temperature | causes=slow permanent deformation
corrosion | is_a=failure mode | occurs_when=metal reacts with its environment | causes=loss of section | causes=weakening of a structure | requires=oxygen | requires=moisture
brittle fracture | is_a=failure mode | occurs_when=a crack spreads before the material yields | causes=sudden failure with no warning
yield point | is_a=stress at which a material stops returning to its shape | purpose=marking where deformation becomes permanent

# --- the things built --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
beam | is_a=structural member | purpose=carrying a load across a span | has_property=in tension on one face and compression on the other
column | is_a=structural member | purpose=carrying a load downwards | causes=load being transferred to the foundation
truss | is_a=structure of triangles | purpose=carrying a load with little material | has_property=members carry only tension or compression
arch | is_a=structure | purpose=carrying a load across a span in compression | causes=an outward thrust at its base | requires=abutments to resist the thrust
suspension bridge | is_a=bridge | purpose=spanning a long distance | has_part=cable | has_part=tower | has_part=deck | has_property=the cables carry the deck in tension
foundation | purpose=spreading the load into the ground | requires=knowledge of the soil
cantilever | is_a=beam fixed at one end only | purpose=projecting over a space with no support beneath it
gear | purpose=changing the speed and torque of a rotation | has_property=trades speed for force
lever | purpose=trading distance for force
pulley | causes=a load being lifted with less effort when several are used
bearing | is_a=machine part | purpose=letting a shaft turn with little friction | causes=less wear | requires=lubrication
lubrication | is_a=practice | purpose=reducing friction between moving parts | causes=less heat | causes=longer life
heat exchanger | is_a=device | purpose=moving heat from one fluid to another without mixing them
pump | is_a=machine | purpose=moving a fluid against a pressure difference | requires=energy | has_part=impeller
turbine | purpose=taking energy out of a moving fluid | causes=rotation of a shaft
control system | is_a=system | purpose=keeping a quantity at a set value | has_part=sensor | has_part=controller | has_part=actuator | requires=feedback
feedback | is_a=signal fed back into a system | purpose=correcting the difference between what is wanted and what is happening | causes=stability when negative | causes=oscillation when the delay is too long
redundancy | is_a=design technique | purpose=keeping a system working when one part fails | causes=higher cost | causes=higher reliability
